{
 "id": "2025-wang-yangzhou",
 "name": "Yangzhou Ancient Canal: Winter and Summer Scenic Beauty",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: participants say whether they have a landscape-architecture education background and give their education level, then rate ten photographs of five sites on the Yangzhou ancient Grand Canal (each in winter and in summer) in the paper's order, No. 1 to No. 10, on the paper's seven-point scale from -3 (strongly dislike) to +3 (strongly like). Rebuilt from Wang, Qian, Cao, Fan & Han (2025), Scientific Reports 15: 7500, with the photographs printed in the paper's Fig. 4 (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0; the figure file is used unaltered and each photo is shown by cropping the view in the browser). Analysis as in the paper: Scenic Beauty Estimation (Daniel & Boster 1976): standardise each judge's scores (z), average the z scores per photo to get its SBE value, and compare winter with summer at each site; the paper then correlated SBE values with colour saturation and colour diversity measured by scene parsing. Differences from the original study: (1) the paper's questionnaire had 17 questions but prints only the photo-rating part; the two background questions here (landscape-architecture background, education level) are our wording, based on the paper's description of its respondents; (2) the photographs come from the published figure, so they are smaller (about 400 x 280 px) than the camera originals; (3) one photo per screen instead of one scrolling questionnaire page.",
